{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Preferences","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides"}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","metadata":{"title":"Preferences","modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}],"role":"collectionGroup"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit’s preference system enables "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"bottom-up data flow"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the reverse of environment values. While the environment passes data down from parent to child, preferences let child views publish values that ancestors can observe and react to."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The system mirrors SwiftUI’s preference API and consists of three parts:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PreferenceKey"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Protocol that defines a named value type with a default and a reduce strategy"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PreferenceValues"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Type-safe storage that holds all preference values for a scope","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"PreferenceStorage","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Stack-based collector that manages preference contexts per render pass"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A built-in example is "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/NavigationTitleKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": a child view sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".navigationTitle(\"Settings\")"},{"type":"text","text":", and the enclosing navigation container reads that preference to render the title bar."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Defining-a-Preference-Key","text":"Defining a Preference Key","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A preference key declares what type of value it carries and how multiple values from sibling children are combined:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct CounterKey: PreferenceKey {","    static let defaultValue: Int = 0","","    static func reduce(value: inout Int, nextValue: () -> Int) {","        value += nextValue()","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defaultValue"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Returned when no child has set this preference"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(value:nextValue:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Combines values when multiple children set the same key"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":" implementation simply takes the last value. Override it when you need additive behavior (summing counts), array collection, or other merge strategies.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Setting-a-Preference","text":"Setting a Preference","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Child views publish a preference using the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".preference(key:value:)"},{"text":" modifier:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct ItemView: View {","    var body: some View {","        Text(\"Item\")","            .preference(key: CounterKey.self, value: 1)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Under the hood, this wraps the view in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PreferenceModifier"},{"type":"text","text":" that calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preferences.setValue(_:forKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" during rendering. The value is reduced into the current scope using the key’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" function."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Observing-Preferences","text":"Observing Preferences","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ancestor views react to collected preferences using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onPreferenceChange(_:perform:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct ItemList: View {","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            ItemView()","            ItemView()","            ItemView()","        }","        .onPreferenceChange(CounterKey.self) { totalCount in","            \/\/ totalCount == 3 (three children each set value: 1, additive reduce)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The modifier pushes a new preference context, renders all children (which set their preferences), pops the context, and fires the callback with the accumulated result.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-Navigation-Title-Shortcut","text":"The Navigation Title Shortcut","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit provides "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/NavigationTitleKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as a built-in preference key with a convenience modifier:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct SettingsPage: View {","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            Text(\"App settings go here\")","        }","        .navigationTitle(\"Settings\")","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationTitleKey"},{"type":"text","text":" uses the default "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" (last value wins), so the deepest child’s title takes precedence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"How-Preferences-Flow-per-Frame","text":"How Preferences Flow per Frame","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Preferences are collected fresh every frame. Here’s the lifecycle within a single render pass:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reset"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RenderLoop.render()"},{"type":"text","text":" calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preferences.beginRenderPass()"},{"type":"text","text":", clearing all callbacks and resetting the stack to a single empty context"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Set","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": As the view tree renders top-down, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PreferenceModifier"},{"type":"text","text":" views call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setValue(_:forKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which reduces values into the current stack frame"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Scope"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OnPreferenceChangeModifier"},{"type":"text","text":" pushes a new context before rendering its subtree, isolating child preferences"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Collect","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": After the subtree finishes, the modifier pops the context (merging into the parent) and fires the callback with the scoped result","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Discard"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": At the start of the next frame, everything resets: stale preferences never persist","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This per-frame reset ensures preferences always reflect the current view tree. Removed views stop contributing automatically."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Reduce-Strategies","text":"Reduce Strategies","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" function determines how multiple children’s values combine. Common patterns:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Strategy","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementation"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use Case"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Last value wins"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"value = nextValue()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (default)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Titles, labels: deepest child wins"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Additive","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value += nextValue()"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Counting items, summing heights","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Array collection","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"value.append(contentsOf: nextValue())","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gathering menu items, breadcrumbs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"code":["\/\/ Array collection example","struct BreadcrumbKey: PreferenceKey {","    static let defaultValue: [String] = []","","    static func reduce(value: inout [String], nextValue: () -> [String]) {","        value.append(contentsOf: nextValue())","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/preferences"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass data from child views up to their ancestors."}],"references":{"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/ListAndTable":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build scrollable, navigable data collections with keyboard support."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"List and Table Components","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/listandtable"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/LayoutSystem":{"abstract":[{"text":"Understand the two-pass layout used by stacks and other layout containers.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem","title":"Layout System","kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/layoutsystem"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/StatusBarGuide":{"title":"Status Bar","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","type":"topic","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/statusbarguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure the shortcut bar at the bottom of the terminal."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/KeyboardShortcuts":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/keyboardshortcuts","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Keyboard Shortcuts","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How keyboard input flows through TUIkit: from raw terminal bytes to your view handlers."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit","kind":"symbol","images":[{"type":"icon","identifier":"tuikit-logo.png"},{"type":"card","identifier":"tuikit-logo.png"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A declarative, SwiftUI-like framework for building Terminal User Interfaces in Swift."}],"title":"TUIkit"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/NavigationTitleKey":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NavigationTitleKey"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A preference key for the navigation title."}],"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/navigationtitlekey","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NavigationTitleKey"}],"type":"topic","title":"NavigationTitleKey","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/NavigationTitleKey"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/ThemingGuide":{"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/themingguide","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Theming Guide","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Customize the visual appearance of your TUIkit application with palettes."}]},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/FocusSystem":{"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/focussystem","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem","abstract":[{"text":"Navigate between interactive elements using the keyboard.","type":"text"}],"title":"Focus System","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/StateManagement":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/statemanagement","abstract":[{"text":"Manage reactive state in your TUIkit application.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"State Management","role":"article"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/AppearanceAndColors":{"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/appearanceandcolors","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Control border styles, visual appearances, and the color system."}],"kind":"article","title":"Appearance and Colors","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/CustomViews":{"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/customviews","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build your own views by composing existing ones or creating custom view modifiers."}],"title":"Custom Views","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"tuikit-logo.png":{"variants":[{"traits":["1x","light"],"url":"\/images\/TUIkit\/tuikit-logo.png"}],"alt":"TUIkit Logo","identifier":"tuikit-logo.png","type":"image"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/PaletteReference":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A visual reference for all built-in color palettes with their exact color values."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Palette Reference","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/palettereference"}}}